+# Coupled run status
+
+Inspect a native run without contacting a provider or running tools:
+
+```text
+spiral coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`PATH` is resolved relative to the caller's current working directory. The installed
+entry point forwards the same command and arguments:
+
+```text
+npm exec spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+The command reads `iterations.json` and durable `state/tui-work.json` ledgers. A wire
+request is every ledger request; a task request is a request whose `charge` is `task`.
+A missing `charge` uses the native default (`task`). Failed and in-flight requests are
+still counted. An interrupted pending ledger may be missing: in that case pending usage
+and aggregate used/remaining values are `null`, rather than being reported as zero.
+
+The status is the recorded native state (`completed`, `stopped`, or `running`). It is
+not an independent verification, qualification, or promotion authorization decision.
+
+The following is the completed synthetic example produced by
+`scripts.status_fixture.make` and represented by `scripts.status_fixture.expected('completed')`:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"status":"completed","stop_reason":"completed","iterations":[{"iteration":1,"task_id":"t1","termination":"completed","task_requests":2,"wire_requests":3,"changed_files":["src/a.rs"],"newly_verified":["cargo test -q"]}],"pending":null,"requests":{"task_used":2,"wire_used":3,"task_limit":192,"wire_limit":216,"task_remaining":190,"wire_remaining":213}}
+```
